WEBVTT

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.850
Nice! Run!

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:15.200
<i>There's no way a girl can
hit my pitches, anyway!</i>

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:19.910
Katahira!

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.500
Yokouchi!

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:24.960
Safe!

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.710
What? Safe?!

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.290
Yokouchi, back home!

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:30.960
What?

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:37.330
Heya.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.440
Yes!

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.450
We took the lead!

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.890
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.890
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.890
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:46.850
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.370
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.370
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.370
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:08.330
<i>As long as you don't throw weak pitches, 
they won't be able to hit anything.</i>

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.170
<i>It's goin' outside again.</i>

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>That's... what I was waitin' for!</i>

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.470
Strike three!

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.280
You're out!

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.680
<i>It...</i>

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.370
<i>It curved?!</i>

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.100
A-A breaking ball?!

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.150
Strike!

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.320
Strike three! You're out!

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.060
I'm glad we got three runs right out the gate.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:46.790
With those sliders in the mix,
we won't be hitting much.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.830
Strike! You're out!

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:53.840
Three outs. Change sides!

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:02.170
Dead ball!

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:05.640
Huh?

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.020
Ball two!

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:11.980
Ball three!

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.720
Ball! Four balls!

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.310
Wh-What are you doing?

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.010
Around here, I guess?

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.070
I'm sure you're nervous too,

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:43.510
but maybe the issue with your 
control is the height of the mound.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:49.780
I checked before the game.
The mound's a bit taller here.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:50.980
What?

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:52.520
Play!

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:58.610
<i>The height of the mound?</i>

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.820
<i>Are ya serious?</i>

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.070
Strike!

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.070
It went in?

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.860
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:25.990
Strike!

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.560
She's starting... to get strikes now.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:31.690
All right!

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.440
Out!

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.370
Yes, a double play!

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:19.750
<b>Backup</b>

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.590
Three outs! Change sides!

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.750
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.750
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.750
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:20.750
We did it! We made it through.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.250
Nice job, Mutsuko.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.210
Yeah!

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.880
What was <i>that</i> about?

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.680
After that timeout,
your control suddenly improved.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.220
It's all thanks to Daigo.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:34.390
He suggested adjusting
the height of the mound.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:37.140
That made my pivot leg more stable,
making it easier to pitch.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.980
That's all?!

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:43.500
You say that like it's minor, but the 
pitching motion starts with the pivot leg.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.570
If something feels off when you pivot,
 it affects everything.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:51.830
That's why I give you exercises that'll
bulk up your core, since your control is weak.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:56.230
If you don't even know that much,
you've still got a long way to go as a pitcher.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:57.550
What'd you say?!

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:00.520
Hey, come on now.
You're leading off the inning, Nishina-kun.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.090
Oh, uh, right.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.550
Thank you.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:08.510
Okay, so Kandori and Anita, you two
are the base coaches this inning.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:09.580
Okay!

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:15.720
Hey, man, I thought we came here to
check out Itsuki's ace. What's the deal?

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:19.690
I never imagined Yokouchi would 
give up three runs in the first inning.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:24.350
When Sakura started, it didn't look good
for her, but she pulled herself together.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:27.650
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:27.650
<b>Urabe Hayato</b>

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:27.650
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:27.650
<b>Suzuki Andy</b>

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:27.160
Fuurin might be girl-heavy,
but their defense is solid.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:31.130
Yeah. I wonder which way this game will turn.

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:35.060
<i>Batting seventh, right field, Nishina-kun.</i>

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.060
All right, let's go.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:37.080
Play!

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.540
<i>Finally. A guy at the plate.</i>

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.880
<i>A guy who's been pushed down
the order by girls, though.</i>

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.460
<i>He must be a total loser!</i>

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.580
Strike!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:54.720
<i>How the heck did ya know, Shigeno-senpai?</i>

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.640
<i>How </i>could<i> ya have known
that was the problem?</i>

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:01.900
<i>Yer advice got Sakura-senpai
back on her feet again.</i>

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.120
<i>Ya made me look like
some know-nothin' catcher!</i>

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.360
Strike. You're out!

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:17.470
<i>Batting eighth, first base, Tanba-kun.</i>

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.120
Strike!

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:24.970
<i>There are no openings to exploit, huh?</i>

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:29.300
<i>Our players have never
even seen a slider like that,</i>

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:34.260
<i>and his fastballs are so on the money,
the strikeouts will come thick and fast.</i>

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.600
Strike!

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.820
<i>But... we can't just roll over and give up.</i>

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.520
<i>Going forward, we'll face tons of pitchers
with breaking balls in their arsenal.</i>

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:50.820
Strike! You're out!

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.280
<i>Batting ninth, left field, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:56.830
No way I'm hitting those.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.940
Tanba-san.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:00.750
Let's pick at least one of
those pitches to swing at.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:05.080
You never know. You might get lucky.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.670
Oh, y-you're right.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:08.550
Sorry.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.950
Since scoring those runs early on,
we've had five consecutive strikeouts.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:14.100
Huh? Seriously?

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.760
It's worse than that.
Nobody's even brushed the ball.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.180
<i>Looks like I don't have to worry
about giving up any more runs.</i>

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:26.650
<i>I'll finish this up real quick so we can
turn the tide and come out on top.</i>

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:35.570
Strike!

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.880
<i>You can't touch me.</i>

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.050
Strike two!

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:05.020
<i>I'd say, out of all of their batters,
this 9th hitter has the sharpest swing.</i>

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:10.610
Ball!

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:14.110
Nice, nice! Good eye!

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:16.660
Ball!

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.560
Two balls, two strikes!

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.120
<i>That was close.</i>

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:23.080
<i>This guy doesn't swing at borderline pitches.</i>

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:26.540
<i>In that case, let's end this with
a slider into the strike zone.</i>

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.500
<i>Gotcha.</i>

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:43.020
Foul ball!

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:45.980
He made contact!

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.900
Seriously?

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.150
<i>Don't look so smug!</i>

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:58.510
Foul!

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.760
He hit it again!

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.600
Strike!

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.000
You're out!

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:14.460
So close!

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.130
Three outs!

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:16.920
Change sides!

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.540
You were so close!

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.600
You really got a read on that slider.

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.550
That last one was dead straight.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:28.040
I couldn't react and foul it off.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.520
I couldn't swing earlier
because of my nerves.

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:34.980
Next time, I'll go all-out too, Captain.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.070
Yes, please do!

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.030
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.030
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.030
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:52.410
Out!

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:54.750
Nice pitching!

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.920
Two outs! Two outs!

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:00.880
<i>Batting seventh, first base, Katahira-kun.</i>

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:00.880
Let's go!

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:04.490
<i>This team don't know how to bat.</i>

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.850
<i>They're swingin' at all
her sliders and sinkers.</i>

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:13.520
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.490
Out!

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:26.630
Seriously?

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:27.840
The hell?! That arm is nuts!

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:29.310
That was scary fast!

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:36.550
<i>I told my guys to go after the breaking balls,
but her pitches are clean and targeted.</i>

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:39.510
<i>Getting hits against
this team won't be easy.</i>

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:44.050
<i>Which means we need at least
one run on the board before Fuurin</i>

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.970
<i>gets used to Yokouchi's pitches.</i>

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:48.430
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:48.430
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:48.430
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:57.580
<i>They oughta've figured out by now 
that she's got two kindsa pitches.</i>

00:11:58.270 --> 00:12:01.360
<i>They'll pick 'n' choose what to swing at
when they go thru' the order again.</i>

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:03.760
Hello.

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:06.070
Bring it!

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:10.800
<i>In the first, I gifted them a walk,
but since then, it's been a no-hit game.</i>

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:16.070
<i>I was worried my pitching
wouldn't be good enough...</i>

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:19.380
Strike!

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:21.860
<i>...but maybe it is after all!</i>

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.710
Catcher!

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:29.420
I got it!

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.220
Out!

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:33.760
I'm sorry.

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:36.500
I thought I aimed for the bottom
of the ball with that swing.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:38.020
What did you expect?

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:40.790
If you hit the bottom
of a fastball, it pops up.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:46.820
They've started throwing fastballs
the second time down the order.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.830
Fuurin's battery is pretty slick.

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:50.830
Nice pitchin'!

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:53.200
Looks like Sakura's found her groove.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:56.790
Yeah. But who knows if she can
keep this up the whole game.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:02.250
<i>Keep it up, Mutsuko.</i>

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.220
First!

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:06.640
Got it!

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:14.430
Safe!

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:16.040
Yeah!

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:18.980
Don't worry about it!

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.150
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:24.110
<i>Batting fourth, pitcher, Yokouchi-kun.</i>

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.050
Yes!

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:24.110
Okay, bring it!

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.310
<i>Damn...</i>

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:32.040
<i>I can't let myself be beaten by a girl,
even if she is kinda cute!</i>

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:39.670
Second!

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.510
Tanba-san...

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.390
Tanba-san!

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:05.810
Hello? Tanba-san!

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:07.350
Tanba-senpai!

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:09.910
Are you all right?

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.480
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.560
That double play would've ended the inning.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.010
What're ya playin' at?

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:16.870
No more back-to-back errors, y'hear?

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:19.880
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.490
<i>Tanba-san's worries are coming to pass...</i>

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:27.840
<i>Batting fifth, third base, Kagaya-kun.</i>

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:26.860
Let's keep it tight!

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.540
Get 'em!

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:31.800
Hit it!

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:34.810
Okay, let's go!

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:38.810
<i>Looks like their first baseman
 is the weak link in their defence.</i>

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:42.270
<i>I want runners on second and third at least.</i>

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:49.250
<i>Aw, rats.</i>

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:50.530
<i>Did I get too much on it?</i>

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:52.950
Third!

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:00.420
<i>It was the final game
last year's team played in.</i>

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:03.710
<i>A make-or-break game
to qualify for Regionals.</i>

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:05.560
Third!

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:07.780
<i>All right!</i>

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:08.690
<i>We win!</i>

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:12.760
<i>We're finally realizing our dreams
of making it to Regionals!</i>

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.030
Throwing yips?

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:32.650
You saw it from the stands too, right?

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.250
Yeah...

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:40.190
Ever since then, at crunch moments,
my throwing deserts me.

00:15:40.190 --> 00:15:45.000
I'll be fine in practice, but in a game, 
my body seizes up and I can't throw straight.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:51.420
That's why I'm asking you
to please take me off first.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:54.530
I won't lose it for the team
if I'm in the outfield.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:56.030
Please, Shigeno!

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:57.130
Not happening.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:16:01.100
We'll overcome your yips one throw at a time.

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:04.150
You can't just try and live with it.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:13.990
Ow, ow, ow.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:21.440
It's all right.

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:25.420
Throwing errors aren't a big deal.

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:30.630
We'll back you up as much as we can.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:34.340
For real?

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.010
That left fielder got there fast!

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:49.070
Out!

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:54.880
Yes, yes, yes!

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:53.990
Nice one, Daigo!

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.110
<i>Shigeno...</i>

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:58.480
Okay, okay!

00:16:58.480 --> 00:17:00.410
That's two outs now! Two outs!

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:05.300
That throw just now...

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:08.330
Shigeno's arm has improved a lot.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:13.550
<i>Batting sixth, right field, Fujioka-kun.</i>

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:15.200
Fujioka!

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.680
We've still got a chance!

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:25.310
Tanba-san!

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.050
Out!

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:31.170
Three outs!

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:32.150
Change sides!

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:34.550
Tanba-san!

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:36.110
Nice play!

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:37.280
Yeah!

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:43.950
Shigeno's play brought that first 
baseman back from the brink.

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:44.960
Yeah.

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:50.130
Foul, foul!

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:55.050
<i>Stop it.</i>

00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:57.510
Foul.

00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.810
<i>Just stop, already!</i>

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.790
<i>Why are you still fighting so hard?!</i>

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.100
<i>We already know they've won!</i>

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.850
<i>Just let the game end already!</i>

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:07.600
Ball!

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:08.820
Ball four!

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:13.840
That side of him hasn't changed one bit.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:14.320
Huh?

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:18.440
You really don't want
a guy like him as your rival.

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:20.460
Yeah.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.500
Here's our chance!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.750
Go, Shigeno-senpai!

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:33.500
It's gone!

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.740
Keep going, keep going!

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.510
Safe! Safe!

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.900
All right!

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:47.680
Not bad, Captain!

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:01.680
<i>Th-This can't be happening!</i>

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.490
<i>We can't lose to a team full of girls!</i>

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:20.720
Out!

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:22.090
That's game!

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:30.560
Awesome!

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:35.530
I mean, really?

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:37.360
Why the hell are they winning?

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:38.990
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:39.570
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:39.570
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:41.820
They beat Itsuki, who're always in the semis,
in a called game after six?

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:44.800
Sakura did pretty well.

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:47.520
I don't know if she'll be pitching next game,

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:50.540
but if we're their opponents,
they won't get such an easy ride.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:51.540
You said it.

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:53.600
Urabe! Andy!

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:54.250
We're going.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.500
Yes, sir.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:59.960
Who woulda guessed we'd be going up
against Shigeno and his team here?

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.930
Before that, we have to make it through
our game. Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:05.730
Yeah, yeah, I know.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.390
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.390
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.390
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
Our next opponent will be either
Seiwa Middle or Koutou Middle.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Yanagawa</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Yanagawa</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Fuurin</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Fuurin</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Koutou</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Koutou</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.100
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:18.730
Urabe and Andy play for Seiwa.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:23.500
No surprise that, even as second-years,
they're pivotal to their team.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:26.030
<b>Moriguchi</b>

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:26.030
<b>Miyada</b>

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:26.030
<b>Urabe</b>

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:26.030
<b>Suzuki</b>

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:26.030
<b>Takahata</b>

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:26.030
<b>Hirai</b>

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:26.030
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:26.030
Ah, I figured ya'd be up here.

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:30.250
Huh? What are you two still doing here?
I said you could go home.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:32.080
And why the heck didya do that?

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:36.840
If ya were plannin' on scoutin' out
the other teams, you shoulda told us.

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:38.370
That's jus' selfish, Captain!

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:41.210
That's right! <i>Really</i> selfish, Captain.

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:44.660
Oh, uh, I just figured you two would be tired.

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:48.390
<b>Koutou</b>

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:48.390
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:46.120
Play!

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:48.060
Let's go!

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:52.660
Urabe's their ace, but he's on third.

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:55.680
Their number 11 is their starting pitcher today,

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:58.860
so there's a high chance Urabe
will pitch against us tomorrow.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:03.090
Doesn't that mean we won't
get to see him pitch today?

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:05.370
He's gotten really tall, though.

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:07.210
What's this? You know this fella?

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:11.030
Yeah. We used to be teammates
back in grade school.

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:13.600
Oh, that reminds me, Shigeno-senpai.

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:16.080
Who's gonna start for us tomorrow?

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:19.080
I know it means pitching back-to-back
games, but Mutsuko's on the mound.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:21.040
We only needed seventy pitches today.

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:22.550
You'll be okay, right?

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:25.650
Yup! I've got more in the tank.

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:26.810
And if we win,

00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:31.010
I'll pitch in the semi-final and the final
the next day, and any game after that!

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:34.560
Ya ain't allowed to pitch 
twice on the same day.

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:40.190
Well, we'll worry about day three
if we make it through tomorrow.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:55.740
Strike! You're out!

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.580
<b>Koutou</b>

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.580
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:57.950
And that's game.

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:00.530
Ten to two.

00:22:00.530 --> 00:22:01.960
They called it in the fifth.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:03.890
Waste o' time.

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:05.940
It ain't like Seiwa was strong.

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:09.190
The other team was jus' weak, makin' error
after error, so we ain't learned a thing.

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:14.090
No, their opponents <i>were</i> weak, for sure,
but there's more to it than that.

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:20.400
Hits

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:20.400
Steals

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:20.400
Sacrifices

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:20.400
Walks

00:22:15.320 --> 00:22:17.030
In just four innings,

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:20.400
they stole eleven times and sacrificed
seven times. That's not normal.

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:22.760
What do you mean?

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:28.850
Seiwa plays hit-and-run, small ball baseball!

00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:03.900
If we want to beat Seiwa,
we have to stop them in their tracks.

00:24:03.900 --> 00:24:08.050
I'm not all that good at pickoffs, though...

00:24:08.050 --> 00:24:09.780
That's why we're doing special training.

00:24:09.780 --> 00:24:12.590
We only have one day, but let's give it a go.

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:14.840
Give it a go, huh?

00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:20.020
This brings back memories of when
I first started practicing pitching.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>Mutsuko's Special Training</b>

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:22.270
Next time: "Mutsuko's Special Training."

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:24.770
Run to the stage of your dreams!
